From 455ca3cdd0c7c0f9e9cf75b3218b5224418059af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kishor Datta Gupta <2458509+kishordgupta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:31:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add TSJEPA detector for time series (experimental)

TSJEPA applies the Joint-Embedding Predictive Architecture to time
series. A sliding window is cut into patches, some patches are hidden,
and a predictor forecasts their latent embeddings from the visible
ones. The latent prediction error of every patch is mapped back to the
timestamps it covers.

`variant` selects the JEPA that trains the network: 'lejepa' (SIGReg on
one shared encoder, the default), 'ijepa' (EMA target encoder),
'tsjepa' (the network of TS-JEPA) or 'tjepa' (the network of T-JEPA on
patch tokens). Masking, scores and training budget are the detector's
own for every variant.

- pyod/models/ts_jepa.py: TSJEPA, on BaseDetector with the time-series
  input validation and the masked-score workflow used by LSTMAD.
  'block' masking uses context on both sides, 'forecast' masking is
  causal. torch is imported lazily, so the module imports without it.
- pyod/models/_jepa_utils.py: the networks of the four variants,
  SIGReg, the EMA update and the mask samplers.
- pyod/test/test_ts_jepa.py: 28 tests; listed in conftest.py with the
  other torch-dependent modules.
- examples/ts_jepa_example.py.
- Docs: API reference entry, model table rows in README.rst and
  docs/index.rst, two bibliography entries, and the
  experimental-detector lists in the time-series guide and the
  benchmark page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
